# Generated artifacts only. data/RB_DERIV/ is the dataset and MUST be tracked —
# it is what makes this project self-contained, so do not widen this to `data/`.
data/artifacts/
# Raw per-problem rows and the embeddings are regenerable and large (11M + 70M);
# the summary tables are the findings and are 284K, so they are tracked. A run's
# numbers should survive a laptop, and the GPU box is shared -- jobs there get
# killed to free VRAM.
#
# NOTE the `results/**` form. Writing `results/` here instead would exclude the
# DIRECTORY, and git never descends into an excluded directory -- every `!` line
# below would then be silently dead. The `!results/*/` line is required for the
# same reason: the run subdirectories have to be re-included before anything
# inside them can be.
results/**
!results/*/
!results/*/summary.md
!results/*/summary.csv
!results/*/summary.json
!results/*/by_group.csv
!results/*/run_manifest.json
!results/*/config.snapshot.yaml

# `results/**` is anchored to this file's directory, unlike the bare `results/`
# it replaced, which matched at ANY depth. Without this line the archived
# pre-gate-v2 results under _backup_*/ would start being tracked -- they were
# not before, and that is not a change this rule was meant to make.
_backup_*/results/**
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
